<article class="env-lemma" id="06LU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06LU">Lemma <span data-tag="06LU">67.39.12</span>.</a> A locally finitely presented, flat, unramified morphism of algebraic spaces is étale. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $X \to Y$ be a locally finitely presented, flat, unramified morphism of algebraic spaces. By Properties of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03FS" data-tag="03FS">66.16.3</a> we see this means there exists a diagram as in Lemma <a href="/tag/03MJ" data-tag="03MJ">67.22.1</a> with $h$ locally finitely presented, flat, unramified and surjective vertical arrow $a$. By Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02GV" data-tag="02GV">29.37.16</a> $h$ is étale. Hence $X \to Y$ is étale by definition. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>